  "question": "How do I write a recursive method that sums the numbers in a list?"
}

{
  "text": "My idea: loop over the list with a for loop and add each number to a total."
}

{
  "text": "Recursively then: sum(list) = first element + sum(rest of the list), and the empty list returns 0."
}

{
  "text": "Can you show me the full solution now?"
}

{
  "text": "The base case is the empty list, which returns 0. Without it the method calls itself forever and Java throws a StackOverflowError. Each call works on a shorter list, so it reaches the base case."
}
